.Dd $Mdocdate: November 9 2026 $
.Dt IMAPIDLE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imapidle
.Nd watch IMAP mailboxes and run mbsync
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm imapidle
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
logs into one or more IMAP accounts, waits for mailbox changes, and runs
.Sy mbsync
for the matching channel.
.Sy mbsync
itself runs once and exits.
.Nm
is the long-running side of that pair.
.Pp
Each account is independent.
A bad password, a refused certificate, a dead server, a failed
.Sy mbsync ,
or a broken mailbox connection is logged and retried later.
It does not stop the other accounts, and it does not exit the process.
The process leaves the main loop only on
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file
Read
.Ar file
instead of the default configuration.
The certificate store is
.Pa known_hosts
in the same directory as
.Ar file .
.It Fl d
Stay in the foreground.
Do not double-fork.
Copy each log line to standard error as well as
.Xr syslog 3 .
Use this to accept a certificate and to watch a run.
.El
.Pp
With or without
.Fl d ,
the first connection attempts happen before a daemon would fork, so a
terminal can still answer a certificate prompt.
Later reconnects are not interactive.
A changed or unknown certificate is refused unless standard input is a
terminal.
Run
.Nm Fl d
once to accept it.
.Pp
Operational messages use
.Xr syslog 3
with ident
.Cm imapidle ,
options
.Cm cons,pid ,
and facility
.Cm mail .
.Pp
.Sy mbsync
is executed as
.Pa /usr/local/bin/mbsync
with the account's channel name as its only argument.
The child waits for that account's
.Va wait
seconds, then replaces itself with
.Sy mbsync .
A non-zero exit is logged.
The IMAP loop does not wait for
.Sy mbsync
to finish.
.Sh IDLE AND NOTIFY
If the server advertises
.Cm NOTIFY ,
.Nm
sends
.Dl NOTIFY SET (personal (MessageNew MessageExpunge MessageFlags))
on the connection it keeps.
One event on that connection runs the account's
.Sy mbsync
channel.
The debounce interval is the smallest interval among that account's folders.
.Pp
Otherwise
.Nm
opens one
.Cm IDLE
connection per folder
.Pq RFC 2177 .
While a connection is in
.Cm IDLE ,
.Nm
sends no other commands on it.
About every 30 seconds it sends
.Cm DONE
and issues
.Cm IDLE
again, which also discovers a dead server.
On
.Cm NOTIFY
connections the same timer sends
.Cm NOOP .
.Pp
The first matching event for a connection starts
.Sy mbsync .
Further events on that connection are logged and ignored until the
debounce interval has passed since that start.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/imapidle/imapidle.conf
Default configuration.
See
.Sy imapidle.conf(5) .
.It Pa ~/.config/imapidle/known_hosts
SHA256 certificate fingerprints accepted for the default configuration.
The file mode is 0600 when
.Nm
creates it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std imapidle
Startup failures, including a missing configuration or a file with no
usable account, exit 1 before the main loop.
After the main loop has started, the process exits 0 on
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT
and otherwise keeps running.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Accept certificates and watch the log on the terminal:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
imapidle -d
.Ed
.Pp
Use a configuration outside the default path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
imapidle -c /home/user/.config/imapidle/imapidle.conf
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Sy imapidle.conf(5)
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Todd T. Fries Aq Mt todd@fries.net
